Data source (web parity):
  useChargingSessionsPaginated(vehicleId, { limit: 200, start, end })
    → GET /charging?vehicle_id&limit=200&offset=0&start&end → ApiChargingSession[]
  The web page fires this one paginated query; the Apple seam mirrors it as
  ChargingCurveDataSource.loadSessions(vehicleID:range:) -> [ChargingCurveSession], bound
  through ChargingCurvePageModel (no networking in the view, ADR-004). The header
  VehicleSelect maps to loadVehicles(); the RangePicker presets map to the query's start/end.

SI discipline (ADR-005): ChargingCurveSession stores energy in watt-hours and power in watts
  (SI canonical, matching the Go JSON tags total_energy_added_wh / peak_power_w / avg_power_w).
  The view converts to the page's fixed kWh / kW display units at the render boundary
  (ChargingCurveFormat, ÷ 1000) — the web sub-components' explicit "kWh"/"kW" targets. Nothing
  non-SI is stored or computed.
  Disclosed deviation (no silent drift): the web `SummaryStatsGrid` "Total Energy" card renders
  `fmtNumber(Σ total_energy_added_wh)` (a Wh sum) under a "kWh" unit label — a latent 1000× label
  mismatch. The native card applies the SI ÷ 1000 so the kWh label is numerically correct
  (ChargingSummaryGrid.energyKwh). Every other stat (avg/peak kW already ÷ 1000 in the web,
  duration, cost, count) mirrors the web computation verbatim. This is the only intentional
  numeric divergence and is corrected toward SI-correctness, not narrowed.

