    ld: warning: ignoring file '.../Shared.framework/Shared': found architecture 'arm64',
        required architecture 'x86_64'
    Undefined symbols for architecture x86_64 / ld: symbol(s) not found for architecture x86_64
  Cause: the `generic/platform=iOS Simulator` destination links a universal (arm64 + x86_64)
  simulator binary, but the gradle-staged KMP `Shared.xcframework` ships only the
  iosSimulatorArm64 slice on this runner. This is an environment/toolchain constraint
  (arm64-only KMP framework), NOT a code defect — no Swift source failed to compile.

  Re-link for the active simulator arch (Apple Silicon = arm64, the slice the framework
  provides; the same arm64-only resolution the macOS build uses, and what the sibling
  Powershare P7 log achieved via a concrete arm64 simulator destination):
